{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Vomited Poison: a past life story","html":"<article id='ja69'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Jātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stories of Past Lives 69 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Itthivagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Women </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>9. Visavantajātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Vomited Poison: a past life story </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Dhiratthu taṁ visaṁ vantaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Curse that vomited poison, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>yamahaṁ jīvitakāraṇā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>which I vomited for the sake of life </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Vantaṁ paccāvamissāmi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and now shall consume again. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>mataṁ me jīvitā varan”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Death is better for me than life! </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Visavantajātakaṁ navamaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
